{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784727419,"nonce":"zoZXLOkeRSUq4D8LoCd5dTVkSTY=","message":"Update: fixed upstream in patatt, via a different mechanism than this bug's original RCA identified.\n\nCorrected root cause. The original RCA blamed Textual's suspend()/event-loop\n(the app supposedly not resuming after the signing exception). That was wrong:\nin the dry-run path the SigningError would have propagated out of the suspend()\nblock, resumed the app, and surfaced via the except -\u003e notify() at\n_review_app.py:1667 as an error, not a freeze. The hang actually happens\n*earlier*, inside the gpg subprocess call, before any exception is raised.\n\nReal mechanism (confirmed, reproduced without a smartcard): patatt ran gpg\nthrough subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True), i.e. with pipe FDs for\nstdout/stderr. gpg auto-starts daemon children (gpg-agent, and scdaemon for a\ncard) that inherit those pipe FDs. Even after gpg itself exits, a lingering\ndaemon keeps the write end open, so subprocess.run's pipe-drain never sees EOF\nand blocks forever. That matches the strace exactly (gpg exit_group(2), then\nPython parked). A revoked/lost key or a misconfigured card is what leaves the\ndaemon lingering. Note this was never TUI-specific -- 'b4 send' on the CLI\nshares the same send_mail -\u003e patatt.rfc2822_sign -\u003e gpg path and had the same\nlatent hang.\n\nFix (upstream patatt, main @ 3a3c141, 'Fix gpg subprocess hang by redirecting\noutput to files', released as 0.7.1). Different approach than the RCA suggested,\nbecause the RCA's target (suspend) was not the cause: _run_command now redirects\ngpg stdout/stderr to tempfile.TemporaryFile() handles instead of capture_output\npipes. With files there is no pipe-drain loop, so subprocess.run returns as soon\nas gpg exits regardless of what a daemon child inherited; pinentry is unaffected\n(it uses the controlling terminal, not stdout). Ships with a pure-Python\nregression test. No b4 code change is required -- Lorenzo's revoked-key case now\nsurfaces as a 'Send failed: ...' notification instead of freezing.\n\nb4 side: the patatt submodule has been bumped from v0.7.0 (b967423) to 3a3c141.\nLeaving this bug open pending the submodule-pointer commit landing on master\n(and any real-world confirmation).","files":null}]}